        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="mb" value="Measured on the same cases&#10;error grows 3.5&#215; along missing days&#10;and 9.6&#215; along peak-window overlap" style="rounded=0;fillColor=#E8F5E9;strokeColor=#2E7D32;fontSize=11.5;fontColor=#1B5E20" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="730" y="446" width="290" height="66" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="law" value="One law, not two regimes:  measure missingness on the support of the estimand.&#10;&#8216;Timing versus length&#8217; is that law at the two ends of a scale; the crossover is at a support width of 91 days.&#10;A support must be located before it can be conditioned on, so the conditioning set is the support dilated by the&#10;year-to-year wander of its own location &#8212; one window of 60 to 90 days serves every warm-season endpoint." style="rounded=1;fillColor=#E3F2FD;strokeColor=#1565C0;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#0D47A1" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="140" y="560" width="840" height="86" as="geometry"/>
